      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Adding basal or long-acting insulin when you are currently low can suppress needed carbohydrate uptake and make your blood sugar drop further. Since you are still unstable, the most important step is to keep treating the low with quick sugars (like a small snack if juice didn't help) and checking your glucose regularly. Because you are alone and still symptomatic, please call a medical helpline or local emergency number to speak with a healthcare professional right away for guidance.",
